From 8b2366feb91a1da72f616405979b954bc80f07a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nhat-Trieu Huynh-Pham <trieu2.huynh@lge.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:35:19 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] sched_ext: minimal Linux 6.1 backport for
 scx_lavd/scx_p2dq/scx_fcp

Backport the sched_ext plumbing required to run the scx BPF schedulers on
android14-6.1: struct_ops sleepable programs and BPF links, kfunc
registration hooks, the ext core and fair.c call sites, and the verifier
relaxation for non-scalar global subprogs.

This is the reduced form of the earlier vendor series:

  - drop the unrelated goldfish address-space/sync driver rewrite and the
    dma-buf heaps Makefile edit, so enabling sched_ext no longer drags in
    unrelated drivers and kernel threads that would perturb measurements
  - drop the VIRTIO/GOLDFISH/USB/CPUFREQ select lines from the
    SCHED_CLASS_EXT Kconfig entry
  - fix bpf_cpumask_populate(), which parsed a text mask from a user
    pointer instead of copying the raw bitmap from BPF memory
  - make bpf_cpumask_any_distribute()/any_and_distribute() actually
    spread picks instead of always returning the lowest CPU

The remaining architectural differences from upstream sched_ext (CFS
hooks instead of ext_sched_class, per-CPU DSQs, single global idle mask)
are documented in review/BACKPORT_MINIMAL_REVIEW.md and must be accounted
for in any measurement comparison.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
